WEBVTT

00:03:30.196 --> 00:03:32.476
OK, relatively shallow in my game.

00:03:33.476 --> 00:03:36.876
All that lovely organic material
comes down and settles there.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.156
And it gets eaten by deep-sea animals.

00:03:39.196 --> 00:03:42.916
Those deep-sea animals are eating it,
they're recycling it, they're burning it.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.956
They’re incorporating into the food chain,

00:03:44.956 --> 00:03:47.156
and they incorporate it
into the sediments.

00:03:47.196 --> 00:03:49.676
So these animals are essentially gardening

00:03:49.716 --> 00:03:51.956
because if they didn't do that,

00:03:51.996 --> 00:03:54.076
these big, vast abyssal
plains of the planet

00:03:54.076 --> 00:03:56.476
would become big,
stagnant, horrible cesspits.

00:03:56.476 --> 00:04:02.036
So the deep-sea animals are basically
irrigating a big chunk of the planet.